  "html": "<p style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(65, 65, 65); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\" id=\"isPasted\"><span style=\"color: rgb(40, 50, 78); font-size: 24px; font-family: Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;\">\ud83d\udcde <strong>CH Information</strong></span></p><p data-pm-slice='1 1 [\"list\",{},\"list_item\",{\"indent\":2,\"type\":\"numbered\"}]' style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 50, 78);\">Continuity of care is really important in this case, as you are helping a couple with fertility issues.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 50, 78);\">Therefore, ideally, both partners should attend together, each having a distinct appointment <span style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 50, 78);\">with the <strong>same</strong> GP. Ideally the appointments should be booked one after the other so appointments can be linked. </span></span></p><p data-pm-slice='1 1 [\"list\",{},\"list_item\",{\"indent\":2,\"type\":\"numbered\"}]' style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 50, 78);\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 50, 78);\">However, if this is not possible, each partner can attend at a convenient time for each.</span></span></p><p data-pm-slice='1 1 [\"list\",{},\"list_item\",{\"indent\":2,\"type\":\"numbered